<section class="section reveal" id="service"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-icon">▦</span><h2>02. What StudyBolt does</h2></div><p>StudyBolt helps you turn course materials into practical study resources, organize your learning, and review topics at your own pace.</p><div class="grid"><div class="mini"><strong>📚 Your study library</strong><span>Organize supported documents, notes, and presentations.</span></div><div class="mini"><strong>📝 Notes & summaries</strong><span>Turn study content into easier-to-review materials.</span></div><div class="mini"><strong>🧠 Flashcards & quizzes</strong><span>Practice concepts, recall and self-testing.</span></div><div class="mini"><strong>◷ Study planning</strong><span>Track sessions, timers, plans and learning progress.</span></div></div><p>Features may vary by platform, device, app version, eligibility, and subscription tier. StudyBolt is intended to support education, not to replace instructors, accredited courses, or independent study.</p></section>
<section class="section reveal" id="accounts"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-icon">♙</span><h2>03. Accounts & security</h2></div><p>You agree to provide accurate account information, keep your login credentials secure, and promptly notify us if you suspect unauthorized access. You are responsible for activities under your account except where the law provides otherwise.</p><p>StudyBolt may support email sign-in or third-party identity providers, depending on the current app configuration. You must follow applicable provider rules as well.</p><p>Do not access another student's account or share an account in a manner that compromises its security.</p></section>
<section class="section reveal" id="materials"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-icon">▤</span><h2>04. Your notes, PDFs & course materials</h2></div><p>You may submit materials such as lecture slides, handouts, class notes, supported PDFs, presentations, and original study content ("User Content"). You retain any ownership rights you already have in your original User Content.</p><p>You confirm that you have the necessary rights or permissions to upload and process your User Content, including any copyrighted textbooks, professor slides, third-party documents, or materials governed by your school's rules.</p><p>You grant StudyBolt a limited, nonexclusive permission to host, store, reproduce, convert, analyze, and display your User Content <strong>only as reasonably necessary to provide, secure, and maintain the features you request</strong>, subject to our Privacy Policy. This does not transfer ownership of your content to StudyBolt.</p><p>Do not upload materials containing another person's sensitive information unless you are permitted to do so. You are responsible for keeping backups of important study materials.</p><div class="note">StudyBolt does not automatically grant you the right to redistribute textbooks, lecture slides, or materials owned by a university, instructor, or publisher.</div></section>
<section class="section reveal" id="ai"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-icon">▣</span><h2>05. AI-generated learning tools</h2></div><p>StudyBolt may use automated technologies and AI services to produce summaries, study notes, flashcards, practice questions, explanations, or other learning resources based on the content you provide.</p><ul><li><strong>Check accuracy.</strong> Outputs can be incomplete, outdated, misleading, or incorrect.</li><li><strong>Use your judgment.</strong> Compare important information against your course materials and instructor guidance.</li><li><strong>Respect your school's policies.</strong> Rules about AI use may vary by course, instructor, institution, or assessment.</li><li><strong>Never assume a guaranteed result.</strong> StudyBolt cannot promise a grade, exam score, admission, certification, or academic outcome.</li></ul><p>Generated content may not be unique to you, and similar inputs may produce similar outputs for other users. You are responsible for reviewing and appropriately using generated materials.</p><p><strong>AI processing disclosure:</strong> See our Privacy Policy for current information on external AI processors, data retention, and whether inputs or outputs are used for model training. [VERIFY THAT THE LINKED POLICY ACCURATELY DESCRIBES PRODUCTION BEHAVIOR.]</p></section>
<section class="section reveal" id="integrity"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-icon">⚖</span><h2>06. Academic integrity</h2></div><p>StudyBolt is designed to help you learn concepts, practice recall, and prepare for assessments. You agree not to use the Service to violate academic honesty rules or engage in prohibited conduct.</p><ul><li>Use AI-generated notes and quizzes as study aids, not as unquestioned sources of truth.</li><li>Follow rules for take-home exams, assignments, citations, collaboration, and AI assistance.</li><li>Do not submit someone else's work as your own or claim generated content is original work where disclosure is required.</li><li>Respect instructors', classmates', and publishers' intellectual property.</li></ul><div class="note"><strong>Study tip:</strong> Use StudyBolt to understand, quiz yourself, and build confidence—not to bypass learning.</div></section>
<section class="section reveal" id="features"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-icon">◷</span><h2>07. Audio, progress & study plans</h2></div><p>StudyBolt may provide audio study tools, text-to-speech, study timers, generated plans, mastery estimates, and progress dashboards. These tools are organizational and educational aids; progress scores and mastery indicators are estimates and not official academic assessments.</p><p>Audio output and synthesized voices may contain pronunciation or content errors. Your ability to use certain functions may depend on device compatibility, operating system support, permissions, available storage, connectivity, or processing limits.</p><p>Back up any work you cannot afford to lose. Device changes, app updates, synchronization issues, or service interruptions may affect locally stored or synchronized content.</p></section>
<section class="section reveal" id="subscriptions"><div class="section-head"><span class="section-icon">◇</span><h2>08. Free features, subscriptions & billing</h2></div><p>StudyBolt may offer free features, paid subscriptions, trials, or usage limits. The app's current purchase screen will explain the relevant plan, price, billing period, features, and any trial terms before you complete a purchase.</p><h3>Automatic renewal</h3><p>If you purchase an automatically renewing subscription, it renews unless canceled according to the applicable app store's rules. Your app store account is generally charged, and renewal pricing and timing are disclosed at checkout.</p><h3>Free trials</h3><p>If an eligible trial is offered, it may convert into a paid subscription unless canceled before the trial expires, as specified by the relevant store. Trial eligibility and availability are determined by the actual offer terms and app store rules.</p><h3>Cancellation & refunds</h3><p>Deleting the app or your StudyBolt account does not necessarily cancel a subscription. Manage or cancel subscriptions through your Apple App Store or Google Play account, as applicable. Refund requests are generally handled by the relevant billing platform under its refund policies, subject to applicable law.</p><p>We may change future prices, plans or features with notice or consent when required. Any changes to an existing subscription are subject to app store rules and law.</p><div class="note">[VERIFY BEFORE PUBLISHING: Remove references to subscriptions or platforms not offered by StudyBolt, and make sure trial and billing disclosures match the live paywall.]</div></section>
